---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Shipping & Returns"
  description="Shipping, production, returns, and order-assistance information for purchases through the Red River Gorge Hiker Store."
>
  <div class="page prose">
    <h1>Shipping & Returns</h1>

    <section>
      <h2>INTRODUCTION</h2>
      <p>Products purchased through the Red River Gorge Hiker Store are made to order and fulfilled through Pixels / Fine Art America. Product configuration, checkout, payment, production, shipping, customer service, and returns are handled through the Store. Please review your product selections carefully before placing an order.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>CHOOSE YOUR OPTIONS CAREFULLY</h2>
      <p>Wall art and other products may offer multiple sizes, print materials, frames, mats, colors, finishes, orientations, and other options. These choices can materially affect both the appearance and final price of your order.</p>
      <p>Please review the product preview, dimensions, material, framing, and all selected options before completing checkout. <strong>The configuration you select in the Red River Gorge Hiker Store is the product that will be manufactured for you.</strong></p>
      <p>If you later decide that you would prefer a different size, frame, material, color, or other configuration, that is generally treated as a normal return rather than a product-quality defect.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>SHIPPING & PRODUCTION TIMES</h2>
      <p>Products are manufactured on demand.</p>
      <p>Art prints, canvas prints, framed prints, metal prints, acrylic prints, wood prints, posters, and jigsaw puzzles are generally <strong>ready to ship within 3–4 business days</strong> after the order is placed.</p>
      <p>Greeting cards are generally <strong>ready to ship within 2–3 business days</strong> after the order is placed.</p>
      <p>These are production estimates, not guaranteed delivery dates. Transit time depends on the destination, carrier, and shipping method selected during checkout.</p>
      <p>The current product-specific production information, shipping options, shipping charges, and delivery information displayed in the Red River Gorge Hiker Store at the time of purchase control the order.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>RETURNS</h2>
      <p>Purchases are covered by the Pixels / Fine Art America return policy. If you are not satisfied with a purchase, it may be returned within <strong>30 days of the order date</strong> in accordance with the Store’s current return procedures.</p>
      <p>After the returned product is received, the product purchase price is refunded under that policy.</p>
      <p><strong>Original shipping charges and return shipping charges are generally not reimbursed. The buyer is responsible for the cost of shipping a non-defective return back to the fulfillment provider.</strong></p>
      <p>Shipping charges may be reimbursed when the return is due to a qualifying product-quality defect.</p>
      <p>For large, framed, or otherwise substantial products, <strong>return-shipping costs can be significant.</strong> Please take particular care when selecting artwork size, print material, frame, mat, finish, and other configuration options before ordering.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="return-start-section">
      <h2>How to Start a Return</h2>
      <p><strong>To start a return, use the Store return form and enter the email address used to place your order and your order number. Follow the return instructions provided by Pixels / Fine Art America before shipping the product back. Under the current return policy, the product purchase price is refunded after the returned item is received.</strong></p>
      <p class="return-start-action-row"><a class="return-start-action" href="https://fineartamerica.com/returnsstep1.html?newrma=true">Start a Return →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>IF THERE IS A PRODUCT-QUALITY PROBLEM</h2>
      <p>If an item arrives damaged, defective, or with another apparent product-quality problem, contact the Store’s customer-service team promptly and follow its instructions before arranging a return.</p>
      <p>The fulfillment provider determines how qualifying quality-defect returns are handled under its current policy.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>ORDER, SHIPPING & RETURN ASSISTANCE</h2>
      <p>Because products are manufactured, shipped, and serviced through the Red River Gorge Hiker Store, order-specific questions—including delivery, damage, returns, refunds, and transaction questions—should be directed through the Store’s customer-service process.</p>
      <p>For questions about Red River Gorge Hiker, the photographs, website content, or the business itself, contact <strong><a href="mailto:Ryan@RedRiverGorgeHiker.com">Ryan@RedRiverGorgeHiker.com</a></strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>CURRENT STORE TERMS CONTROL</h2>
      <p>This page summarizes the fulfillment and return terms applicable to purchases made through the Red River Gorge Hiker Store.</p>
      <p>If the fulfillment provider changes its policies, or if product-specific information displayed in the Store differs from this summary, the current terms and information presented by the Store at the time of purchase control the transaction.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
